 sample, or full configuration schema, or if the returned chunks are not detailed enough, call `get_documents(names=[\"documents/...\"])` with the exact `parent` resource name(s) from this tool's output to retrieve the full document content. If 1-2 searches return no relevant results for a specific named feature, API, or setting, stop searching (do not fall back to `answer_query`, which uses the same corpus) and inform the user that it is not documented in the official corpus rather than guessing or fabricating details. When answering the user, always cite the authoritative source document resource names (`documents/...`) or corresponding `https://` URIs.\n","inputSchema":{"description":"Request schema for `search_documents`. Use the `query` field to search for related Google developer documentation.","properties":{"query":{"description":"Required. The raw query string provided by the user, such as \"How to create a Cloud Storage bucket?\".","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"name":"search_documents","outputSchema":{"$defs":{"DocumentChunk":{"description":"A DocumentChunk represents a piece of content from a Document in the DeveloperKnowledge corpus. To fetch the entire document content, pass `parent` in the `names` list of `get_documents(names=[\"documents/...\"])`.","properties":{"content":{"description":"Output only. The content of the document chunk.","readOnly":true,"type":"string"},"id":{"description":"Output only. The ID of this chunk within the document. The chunk ID is unique within a document, but not globally unique across documents. The chunk ID is not stable and may change over time.","readOnly":true,"type":"string"},"parent":{"description":"Output only. The resource name of the document this chunk is from, in the format `documents/{uri_without_scheme}` (corresponding to the web URI `https://{uri_without_scheme}`). Pass this value in the `names` list of `get_documents(names=[\"documents/...\"])` to retrieve the full document. Examp